00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:25.248
At Vancouver's law courts on Friday, dealer Ryan Martin said a business that worked for years has wrecked his family.

00:02:25.788 --> 00:02:31.708
Global news reports that his company, Arctic Machinery, with shops in Prince George, Chilawak, and Kalona,

00:02:32.008 --> 00:02:36.628
started selling machines from Chinese state-owned manufacturer XemG in 2017.

00:02:37.228 --> 00:02:42.388
He said the trade was good until about 2021. His words were, it's destroyed our family.

00:02:43.008 --> 00:02:45.888
XemG is one of the world's largest heavy equipment makers.

00:02:45.888 --> 00:02:48.908
Martin said the quality later was not what it had been.

00:02:49.348 --> 00:02:52.388
Civil suits now alleged the company defrauded dealers in Canada.

00:02:52.828 --> 00:02:55.148
He said other Canadian dealers found the same trouble.

00:02:55.588 --> 00:03:00.208
What they describe in his account is a process of changing serial number plates and changing

00:03:00.208 --> 00:03:03.768
the years of the machines so an end user might not know what they were buying.

00:03:04.268 --> 00:03:08.468
His example was a machine built in 2020 and sold to the dealer as a 2022.

00:03:09.188 --> 00:03:14.208
In July, a Saskatchewan dealer sued, alleging unlawful tampering with serial plates on equipment

00:03:14.208 --> 00:03:19.848
sold and Alberta this year. LTR equipment in Quebec filed a similar case. An Ontario

00:03:19.848 --> 00:03:23.708
lift company has also filed, alleging serial numbers were tampered with.

00:03:24.736 --> 00:03:30.156
XemG Canada told Global News that Arctic machinery purchased approximately $18 million in

00:03:30.156 --> 00:03:35.676
XemG branded inventory and did not pay for it. The company said it is fully defending the claims

00:03:35.676 --> 00:03:40.916
in the civil actions. Martin said the family firm was forced into bankruptcy when XemG called

00:03:40.916 --> 00:03:44.096
in its loans, which he called retaliation for blowing the whistle.

00:03:44.736 --> 00:03:47.416
These are allegations and a defense, not a conviction.

00:03:48.116 --> 00:03:52.736
RCMP and Alberta's K-Division confirmed that the auto theft unit executed a search warrant

00:03:52.736 --> 00:03:56.836
at XCMG headquarters in April, and that the investigation is still going.

00:03:57.336 --> 00:03:59.696
For Arctic machinery, the fight is already a bankruptcy.

00:04:00.316 --> 00:04:04.136
